  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d7e06131-e6b8-4769-bd25-6690fb0a29de-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 184px;\" /></p><p>Using current division rule,&nbsp;</p><p>Current,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p><p>Now, using Kirchhoff&#39;s voltage law- in lower loop,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>i</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math></p><p>Potential difference between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>150</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>275</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
